WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.482
Hi! In editing, besides spelling, there are grammar mistakes too. Today we'll learn a checklist to help you spot them quickly.

2
00:00:10.632 --> 00:00:19.818
First, check the tense. Is the sentence about the past, present or future? Look for time words like yesterday, every day or tomorrow.

3
00:00:19.968 --> 00:00:26.298
Second, check subject-verb agreement. A singular subject needs a singular verb.

4
00:00:26.448 --> 00:00:33.450
Third, check plurals. Many and several need plural nouns, and remember the irregular plurals.

5
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.978
Fourth, check the articles: a, an or the.

6
00:00:37.128 --> 00:00:43.938
Fifth, check prepositions, such as good at, afraid of and interested in.

7
00:00:44.088 --> 00:00:52.386
Let's look at examples. Yesterday, Tom go to the library. Yesterday means past tense, so go becomes went.

8
00:00:52.536 --> 00:00:58.986
Each of the boys have a book. The subject is each, which is singular, so have becomes has.

9
00:00:59.136 --> 00:01:05.442
There are many childs in the park. Child has an irregular plural, so it becomes children.

10
00:01:05.592 --> 00:01:11.610
She is good in maths. We say good at, so in becomes at.

11
00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:15.186
Watch out! A hour is wrong!

12
00:01:15.336 --> 00:01:21.642
The h in hour is silent, so the word starts with a vowel sound. We use an: an hour.

13
00:01:21.792 --> 00:01:28.770
On the other hand, uniform starts with u but sounds like you, so we say a uniform.

14
00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:38.826
Your turn! My sister watch TV every evening. What's wrong? Pause and think.

15
00:01:38.976 --> 00:01:46.794
Watch should be watches, because my sister is singular and it's a daily habit. Did you get it right?

16
00:01:46.944 --> 00:01:56.514
Another one! The cat ran after two mouses. What's wrong? Pause and think.

17
00:01:56.664 --> 00:02:03.858
Mouses should be mice. Mouse has an irregular plural. Did you get it right?

18
00:02:04.008 --> 00:02:13.530
Here's another! Ali is afraid from the dark. What's wrong? Pause and think.

19
00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:19.746
From should be of. We say afraid of. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:19.896 --> 00:02:29.274
One more! She bought a umbrella yesterday. What's wrong? Pause and think.

21
00:02:29.424 --> 00:02:36.330
A should be an, because umbrella starts with a vowel sound. Did you get it right?

22
00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:46.290
And another! Tomorrow, we visited our grandparents. What's wrong? Pause and think.

23
00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:53.538
Visited should be will visit, because tomorrow is about the future. Did you get it right?

24
00:02:53.688 --> 00:03:04.410
Remember the checklist: tense, agreement, plurals, articles and prepositions. Find the time words and the subject first, then check each one.

25
00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:10.362
After correcting, read the sentence aloud to hear if it sounds right!

